Subject: no success acknowledgements on a connection without multiplexing

rsync_uploader_ack_complete() sends IT_SUCCESS for finished files. When
the client is the receiver (a pull, over ssh or rsync://), its writes are
not multiplexed and io_write_buf_tagged() asserts iotag == IT_DATA, so a
pull aborted after its first finished file (NOTES N6). Seen on VMS; the
code path is not VMS-specific. Skip the acknowledgements there.

--- a/uploader.c	2026-11-06 15:13:50.846898784 +0000
+++ b/uploader.c	2026-11-06 15:13:50.867162981 +0000
@@ -1865,6 +1865,15 @@
 		return;
 
 	/*
+	 * Acknowledgements are tagged messages, which the io layer
+	 * allows only on a multiplexed connection: a client receiving
+	 * from a remote sender (a pull) writes without multiplexing,
+	 * and asserted here after its first finished file.
+	 */
+	if (!sess->mplex_writes)
+		return;
+
+	/*
 	 * We'll halt at the next file the uploader needs to process
 	 * since the status of flist entries after that are irrelevant.
 	 */
